# What a player's copilot is asked when its player hands the aircraft to the
# AI with a model chosen to plan it (glideslope --hand-over-model, and
# glideslope_cli connect's). It is told, besides, where the aircraft is, how
# it is flying and the runways near it, as it always is, and answers with a
# route the server checks and flies - nothing else. Lines beginning # are
# comments; the rest is the words.
I have handed you the aircraft in flight while I am away from the controls.
Keep it safe and near: from where it is now, at a safe height above the
ground, fly to somewhere close by worth seeing and orbit over it until I take
the aircraft back.
